# Cloudflare Pages response headers (Next copies public/ → out/; CF Pages reads
# out/_headers). The docs moved off GitHub Pages SO THIS ORIGIN CAN SEND THESE:
# the live-editor <iframe> (play.paged.media) uses SharedArrayBuffer, and SAB needs
# the PARENT page cross-origin-isolated too — which GitHub Pages can't do.
#
# COEP: credentialless (NOT require-corp) is deliberate — it still makes the page
# cross-origin-isolated, but lets cross-origin subresources that DON'T send CORP
# (GA4 / googletagmanager gtag.js, any external image/embed) load credential-less
# instead of being BLOCKED. require-corp would break GA4 and any third-party asset.
#
# ── FIRST-DEPLOY COEP AUDIT (do before cutting docs.paged.media DNS) ───────────
# Load every page type on the *.pages.dev preview URL with these headers on and
# watch the console for "blocked by Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy" — the live
# preview (same-origin wasm ✓), self-hosted fonts ✓, and GA4 (credentialless ✓)
# should all load. Add `crossorigin`/CORP only if the audit finds a blocked asset.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: credentialless
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

# The live-preview wasm must keep its correct MIME for streaming compile.
/preview/*
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
